MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_001: The dirty laundry's really piled up... It's going to\ntake time to wash.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_002: I'll help, Buccar! Want me to carry this heap of\nclothes over there?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_003: Ah, yes. Thanks.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_004: Ahh, nice and tidy! Feels great. Anything else I can\nhelp with?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_005: Hmm...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_006: What's the matter? Did I say something weird?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_007: No, it's just interesting how, ever since we met,\nyou've tried to befriend me.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_008: Between my battle scars and my burn scars,\nI'm more used to being feared.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_009: Huh! I've never thought you were scary.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_010: I didn't have much time with my dad... Maybe I see\nyou as sorta filling in for him.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_011: But there is only one man who you can call\nyour father.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_012: I'd prefer you thought of me as an instructor rather\nthan a parent.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_013: In Cydonia, my reputation for instruction earned me\nthe nickname "Demon Bear of Baphos."
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_014: Wow. I didn't know. That's amazing!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_015: My students were about the same age as you are,\nall of them youths of great potential.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_016: I took careful note of their traits and tailored my\nlessons for each of them.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_017: Wow, you changed your approach for each of them!\nCan you make one for me?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_018: That would be difficult. I'm afraid you are much\nslighter than my students were.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_019: Whaaat? Buccar, c'mon—I want you to train me!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_020: I cannot and will not. The regimens I devise are\ntoo strenuous.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_021: Besides, frankly, I'm opposed to you fighting in the\nfirst place.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_022: Your knowledge of medicinal herbs is vast. You can\ncontribute sufficiently in a support role.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_C_023: Ugh! You're no fun.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_001: Mu! Are you alright?!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_002: Ah, Buccar? Yeah...a little dizzy, but I'm OK.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_003: I'm relieved. But what happened?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_004: The person treating you said you'd gotten heatstroke\nfrom long-term exertion outside.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_005: Surely you know that moving around too much in\nthe sun will make you faint?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_006: Uh...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_007: I see. You've done something that you think is going\nto make me angry.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_008: Well, I...um...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_009: You have that look in your eyes. The same one my\nstudents had when they did something wrong.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_010: The truth is...I went through your stuff and looked at\nthe papers.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_011: Th-the training methods I wrote in Cydonia!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_012: Yeah. It was, uh...five hundred swings with a sword,\nan axe, and a spear, to learn them all equally.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_013: How foolish. That was devised for an experienced\nsoldier of imposing strength!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_014: Ngh... S-sorry...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_015: What's done is done, I suppose. Though I don't\nunderstand why you kept going until you fainted.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_016: I thought if I quit, you'd think I could never do it.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_017: I wanted to surprise you by getting waaay stronger.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_018: I wanted you to smile like my dad, and pat me on the\nhead, and tell me I did OK...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_019: I said it before. I am not your father.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_020: That said, I'm not without blame. It was careless to\nleave my papers where you could see them.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_021: Alright. I will devise a training regimen that\nsuits you.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_022: You mean it? I thought you said you wouldn't.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_023: I don't want to leave you to your own devices and\nhave you do something reckless again.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_024: By my name as Demon Bear of Baphos, I will devise\na training method for you.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_025: Abide by it, and I agree to disregard that you\nviolated my wishes.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_026: Ooh! Hooray! Thanks, Buccar!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_027: Settle down! You're still recovering. You must rest!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_B_028: Headstrong, this one. It may be challenging to teach\na pupil like her.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_001: Hah! Hyaah!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_002: Buccar! What did you think of those moves?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_003: You've improved greatly. You hardly seem like the\nsame person I saw fighting before.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_004: All because of your training, Buccar! Thanks!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_005: No, not entirely. It's due to your own aptitude\nas well.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_006: To think such strength lay in such a slight frame.\nI was negligent to underestimate you.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_007: Were you a new recruit in old Cydonia, you'd have\nbeen welcomed with open arms.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_008: You mean that? Gosh. That's such high praise,\nI'm almost embarrassed.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_009: Still, I feel like I can get way stronger than this.\nSo you'd better keep teaching me!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_010: Your enthusiasm and earnestness give me high hopes\nfor your future.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_011: What do you say, Mu? Would you care to serve\nLady Leda alongside me?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_012: Wha?! Like—as partners?!
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_013: You needn't fear that you're too rambunctious. In my\nyouth, I was much the same, yet I grew into the role.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_014: The most important traits in a knight are valor and a\nloyal spirit. You're not lacking for either.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_015: Besides, it would put me at ease knowing you're by\nLady Leda's side when I can't be.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_016: Woohoo! You really think I'm good.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_017: I can see it now—you as the young, strapping\nattendant kneeling beside milady...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_018: Uh...Buccar? Hey. HEY! You still with me?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_019: You'll grow into a superb young knight. Blessed with\ncharm and grace, you'll receive much praise...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_020: and suitors aplenty who want your hand. Hmmm.\nYou'd better watch out for men deceiving you.
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_021: Why would you bring that up? I'm glad you're\nconcerned for me, sure, but I mean...
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_022: Of course I'm concerned! You must consult me before\nyou agree to a life partnership. Do you hear me?
MID_SE_Buc_Moo_A_023: Hehe... Who was it that said you aren't my dad?